    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule in the owner creation flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a check that rejects the create with **HTTP 409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, placed alongside the existing conflict checks (telephone/household) before the owner is saved.\n- Added a helper `isCityAtCapacity(String city)` that counts existing owners in that city case-insensitively (consistent with the existing `nextCustomerCode` logic) and returns true at `>= 50`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
